1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:05,370
It wasn't until I was sitting in the airport, in the plane, that my nephew called and said,

2
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:10,330
Aunt Steph, it was a white supremacist. He filmed the entire thing on live stream.

3
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:17,150
I groaned and roared and screamed so loudly that the plane was delayed and taking off.

4
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:24,670
I roared in pain for my sister, my beautiful sister, pharmacist, who was serving in the east side.

5
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:29,810
I never knew if I would see her again. I roared also in pain.

6
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:36,370
For my brothers and sisters, who do not look like me, or like the defendant.

7
00:00:37,410 --> 00:00:41,270
I roared in pain because he bought into the lies of this country,

8
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:46,650
that somehow, because of the amount of the chemical in our skin, we are superior.

9
00:00:47,930 --> 00:00:51,910
We were not even the first ones here, in the U.S.

10
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,450
Okay?

11
00:00:53,450 --> 00:01:02,050
Our black and brown brothers and sisters endured centuries, not years, centuries of oppression

12
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:09,050
as they built our buildings and produced our crops, by which the foundation of this country was built on.

13
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:14,380
They continue to endure oppression.

14
00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:22,460
Even the Harvard lawyer is mistaken continually in the courtroom for the defendant and not the lawyer.

15
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,000
They continue to endure microaggressions.

16
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:32,360
They continue to have their families gunned down simply because of the color of their skin.

17
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:40,240
You heard some of the family members today reading from the Bible, offering forgiveness, offering peace,

18
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,540
showing the beauty of their hearts.

19
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,520
Yes, you also saw the fury.

20
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:49,560
And for those who serve, who have to ask people to sit,

21
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:53,280
I ask you to do it with an empathy in your heart and an understanding

22
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:56,760
that for hundreds and hundreds and hundreds of years,

23
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:01,000
we have been looking at our brown brothers and sisters as if they were less than.

24
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:03,280
They are not less than.

25
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:05,000
They deserve our respect.

26
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:07,100
They deserve our radical empathy.

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,780
They deserve for us to get educated on what we can do to treat them with the respect that they deserve.

